==============================================================================
PART D -- exact (not crude) support of D = M - gamma*k
==============================================================================
M ~ Bin(k,gamma) so M in [0,k] exactly (integer-valued, but the
*range* of the real number D=M-gamma*k is exactly the closed
interval [-gamma*k, (1-gamma)*k] -- attained at M=0 and M=k
respectively. This is EXACT, not a bound -- it is what M's own
definition as a Binomial count directly gives, requiring no
further argument.

Contrast with the Bulk/Tail Lemma's existing crude tail-region use
of |D| <= k (i.e. the symmetric interval [-k,k]), which is a valid
but strictly looser superset whenever gamma != 1/2 -- e.g. gamma=0.01
gives true D in [-0.01k, 0.99k], NOT [-k,k]; gamma=0.99 gives true D
in [-0.99k, 0.01k], NOT [-k,k]. This asymmetry is exploited in script 02.
